  "body": "Found while handling uratmangun2 on X (2026-11-06: \"i need to update it every minute\").\n\nThe desktop app's auto-update interval can be set to 24h, through Settings → About → Check every or `magpie update auto 24h`. But the time of the last check is held only in memory. Each relaunch checks again straight away, and offers whatever was tagged since. A user who relaunches often still sees a new version many times a day.\n\nExpected: the last check time is persisted, for example next to the update settings, and a relaunch inside the interval doesn't check. A failed read of it counts as unknown, so the app checks.",
  "closed_by": null,
