   "body": "A fix is on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5528-persist-update-check-time), commit [63e205b14](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/63e205b1449df5bb3aab2ea45ddbd8847979fb96), based on `ed0ab567`.\n\nDesktop and `magpie web` now store the last check time locally beside settings and use it after relaunch with the currently configured interval. Missing, unreadable, invalid or future timestamps count as unknown and cause a check; write errors are logged. A manual check still runs immediately and resets the clock. The timestamp is local state and is not included in the checked backup/sync bundle.\n\nA fake update feed and separate processes reproduce two checks on two launches with the original scheduling behavior and one with the fix. The final test also covers the 24-hour interval, expiry, manual checks and invalid, future or unreadable timestamps. Parent GUI/CLI checks pass under `-race`; vet, formatting and full `nogui` build pass. The old scheduler was extracted unchanged for the controlled red check; no live feed, full suite or Windows runtime was tested. Check-start serialization prevents overlapping disk writes, while state readers do not wait for that disk write. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
