     "body": "### magpie version\n\n0.1.4170 (portable exe downloaded today at 19:51) → 0.1.4176 (installed copy)\n\n### Where\n\nGUI (desktop app serving the gateway on 127.0.0.1:3425), Windows installed layout\n\n### OS\n\nWindows 10 22H2, build 19045.7846, WebView2 Runtime 157.0.4341.46\n\n### What happened\n\nBefore today this machine ran Magpie as a single portable exe at G:\\All Program\\magpie-windows-amd64.exe — no install folder, no AppHang records. Today, after starting 0.1.4170 at 19:51, the app created G:\\All Program\\magpie at 19:55:52 (magpie.exe, magpie.com, webview-profile) and wrote HKCU\\Software\\magpie InstallLocation = G:\\All Program\\magpie. That matches commit 14807bcf (\"update: a Windows download kept outside Downloads asks to install too\", 2026-11-14 10:20 UTC, included in 0.1.4170).\n\nAfter that install, Windows Application log recorded 4 AppHangB1 events this evening:\n\n| time (UTC+8) | process | version |\n|---|---|---|\n| 20:08:18 | G:\\All Program\\magpie-windows-amd64.exe.old-3 (pre-install portable process) | 0.1.4159.0 |\n| 20:30:59 | G:\\All Program\\magpie\\magpie.exe.old | 0.1.4170.0 |\n| 21:02:50 | G:\\All Program\\magpie\\magpie.exe.old | 0.1.4174.0 |\n| 21:40:58 | G:\\All Program\\magpie\\magpie.exe.old | 0.1.4175.0 |\n\n%LOCALAPPDATA%\\magpie\\logs\\app.log contains four full goroutine dumps whose goroutine 1 frames match #5922 exactly:\n\n~~~\ngoroutine 1 ... [running, locked to thread]:\nruntime.throw(...)\n    runtime/panic.go:1229\nruntime.exitsyscall()\n    runtime/proc.go:4888\nruntime.cgocallbackg(...)\n    runtime/cgocall.go:350\n...\nruntime.stdcall(...)\n    runtime/os_windows.go:968\nruntime.exit(...)\n    runtime/os_windows.go:546\nruntime.main()\n    runtime/proc.go:329\n~~~\n\nIn three of the four handovers, the new instance also logged:\n\n~~~\ngateway: http://127.0.0.1:3425 is taken but doesn't answer as magpie yet\ngateway: port 3425 is held by magpie.exe.old (pid ...)\nmagpie: failed to notify first instance: ... profile folder ... held by another process: true\n~~~\n\nThe log between 07:55 and 21:41 contains 31 distinct versions (0.1.4070 → 0.1.4176) and 56 \"started (app)\" lines. After the install, every update cycle leaves another AppHangB1; there were no AppHang records in the previous 14 days, and all four dumps appeared after 19:55.\n\n### Relation to #5922\n\nThe crash stack is exactly the same as in #5922. But #5922 was reported from the portable layout and does not mention the install-folder switch; the new trigger here is the 0.1.4170 self-install behavior (commit 14807bcf). In internal/gui/app.go, when update.Settle() hits, it calls update.Forward() and then returns nil directly instead of going through handover.go's leave/quitBy quit path. That may be why the install handover has no quit deadline and the old process stays in ExitProcess (not verified on a real desktop, just a code-level observation).\n\n### Expected\n\n- The self-install handover and subsequent auto-updates should let the old process exit within a bounded time and release 127.0.0.1:3425 and the WebView2 profile first.\n- At minimum, the installed copy should not freeze on every 30-minute auto-update.\n\nI can provide the full redacted dumps if useful.\n",
